---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Service terms for the mdbase.dev website and mdbase Connect, including the Free and Plus plans."
  contents
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="page-intro__lede">Terms for the public website and the Connect service, including paid plans.</p>
  </header>
  <article class="legal">
    <h2>Open source materials</h2>
    <p>
      The mdbase specification and open source software are provided under the
      licenses stated in their repositories. Those licenses govern source code,
      conformance fixtures, examples, and documentation distributed with the
      projects.
    </p>
    <h2>Who provides Connect</h2>
    <p>
      mdbase Connect is provided by MDBASE (ABN 88 767 454 765), an Australian
      business. Contact us at
      <a href="mailto:support@mdbase.dev">support@mdbase.dev</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Open beta</h2>
    <p>
      mdbase Connect is pre-release software. Availability, storage, routing,
      and account features may change before a stable release. Keep independent
      backups of important collections. Treat the open beta as a working copy
      of data. The service has no availability or data-retention guarantee.
    </p>
    <h2 id="plans">Plans and payment</h2>
    <p>
      Every account starts on the Free plan. New accounts also get extra
      storage for their first 30 days. The Plus plan is a subscription, billed
      monthly or yearly. The <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> lists each
      plan’s price and limits. Accounts created during the beta keep their beta
      allowance.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plus is sold through Link, a Stripe service, which acts as the seller and
      merchant of record. Link takes payment, calculates and collects any sales
      tax, VAT or GST, and sends receipts. Link’s own terms apply to the
      purchase. Plus renews automatically at the end of each billing period
      until you cancel. Switching between monthly and yearly takes effect
      immediately, with the unused part of your current period credited towards
      the new one.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a renewal payment fails, Plus continues for 7 days while you update
      your payment method, then ends.
    </p>
    <h2 id="cancellation">Cancellation and plan changes</h2>
    <p>
      Cancel Plus at any time with <strong>Manage billing</strong> on your
      account page, or from your Link account. Plus continues until the end of
      the period you’ve paid for and doesn’t renew. An account with Plus that is
      set to renew can’t be deleted until you cancel.
    </p>
    <p>
      When Plus or the storage trial ends, your account returns to the Free
      plan’s limits. Nothing is deleted. Collections and files you already have
      stay and keep syncing. While you’re over a limit, you can’t upload new
      files or add collections.
    </p>
    <h2 id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      If you ask within 14 days of a Plus payment, by emailing
      <a href="mailto:support@mdbase.dev">support@mdbase.dev</a> or through
      <a href="https://support.link.com/topics/sold-through-link">Link support</a>,
      we’ll refund that payment and Plus ends. After 14 days, payments aren’t
      refunded, except as required by law. Cancelling stops future renewals but
      doesn’t refund the current period.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes to prices and these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We’ll email you at least 30 days before a price change applies to your
      subscription, and before a change to these terms that affects a paid
      plan. A price change takes effect at your next renewal after that notice.
      If you don’t agree, cancel before then.
    </p>
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Use the service within applicable law and granted access. Authorized
      security testing must stay within its agreed scope. Interference with
      other users and bypassing application grants or collection authority
      checks are prohibited.
    </p>
    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Pre-release services carry no warranty to the extent permitted by law.
      Open source components retain the warranty terms in their respective
      licenses.
    </p>
    <h2>Consumer law</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any right or
      remedy you have under the Australian Consumer Law or other consumer
      protection law that can’t lawfully be excluded.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
